        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): use truncateUtf16Safe for OpenAI tool call id truncation",
        "body": "## What This Problem Solves\n\n`normalizeToolCallId` in `openai-completions.ts:1052` truncates oversized tool call IDs with `id.slice(0, 40)`. When a tool call ID contains a UTF-16 surrogate pair straddling positions 39-40, `slice` splits the pair and leaves an unpaired high surrogate at position 39 — producing invalid Unicode.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nJavaScript `String.slice(0, n)` operates on code units, not characters. A surrogate pair occupies 2 code units. If the cut point falls between the high and low surrogate, the result ends with an unpaired `\\uD800-\\uDBFF` that downstream consumers (OpenAI API, JSON encoding, DB storage) may reject or mangle.\n\n`truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` already exists in the repo and handles this case correctly by moving the boundary to avoid splitting a surrogate pair.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAffects `openai` provider multi-model conversations where tool call IDs are re-normalized (`!isSameModel` → `normalizeToolCallId`). A 40+ character tool call ID with a surrogate pair near position 40 would produce invalid Unicode. This is rare but deterministic; IDs at exactly the wrong length with characters above U+FFFF near the boundary trigger it.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Exact head\n\n```\norigin/main: ec3eb573bf4 test(shared): add unit tests for numeric coercion helper (#98663)\n```\n\n### Format check\n\n```\n$ oxfmt packages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.ts packages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.test.ts\nFinished in 85ms on 2 files using 8 threads.  # no changes, clean\n```\n\n### Diff check\n\n```\npackages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.ts      | 3 ++-\npackages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.test.ts | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++\n2 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n```\n\n### Test output (47/47 passed)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  47 passed (47)\n```\n\n### Mutation check\n\nRevert fix → 1 test fails:\n```\nFAIL  openai-completions.test.ts > openai-completions stop-reason tool-call guard\n     > truncates an oversized tool call id without cutting a surrogate pair\nAssertionError: expected false to be true\n ❯ openai-completions.test.ts:1692:45\n```\n\nRestore fix → 47 passed.\n\n### Collision check\n\nNo competing PRs for this exact fix. Related Unicode-repair PRs on different surfaces: #104054 (HTML tool preview emoji), #107664 (tool arg boundary emoji), #109561 (firecrawl truncation), #109498 (label-open-issues truncation), #109839 (provider error body truncation). None touch `openai-completions.ts:1052` or the `normalizeToolCallId` path.\n\n### Not tested\n\n- Real OpenAI API roundtrip with surrogate-containing tool call IDs (needs API key)\n- Other provider paths (`id.includes(\"|\")` branch) — already uses `replace` + `slice`\n- Non-OpenAI model providers — `normalizeToolCallId` only applies when `model.provider === \"openai\"`\n\n🤖 Generated with [co-mind](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "fix/openai-tool-call-id-utf16-truncation",
